## project-standard

```yaml
adopted: <!-- TODO(project-standard): the commit where this repo adopted the standard -->
direction: docs/NORTH_STAR.md
critical-paths:
  # Paths where a wrong call ships a fabricated result — honesty, scoring,
  # pricing, auth. Declaring none is a valid answer for many repos.
  #
  # An entry may also name what must be READ before editing that path:
  #
  #   - path: src/integrations/
  #     reference: docs/reference/FIELD_MAP.md
  #
  # A bare path says "be careful here". A reference says where the knowledge
  # is, which is the part a newcomer — or an agent — cannot guess. Use it for
  # the lookup that would have prevented a defect, not for background reading:
  # a contract, a generated field map, an ownership register. The checker
  # verifies the file exists and can say whether it is current; it cannot make
  # anyone read it.
```
